task: optics-fuse-reads
agent: opus-optics
started: 2026-09-10
branch: feature/fuse-reads
worktree: ../okay-wt-fusereads
spec: specs/optics.md (stage 10)

why: the operator read "get, foldMap and traverseOf are not fused —
  simply not attempted" and said: attempt them.

what: the write side emits the update; the read side should emit the
  projection. For a lens chain `get` IS `s.a.b`, `foldMap(f)` is
  `f(s.a.b)`, and `traverseOf(f)` is `fmap(f(s.a.b), b => put(s, b))`
  with the put the fusion already emits. A shape with a prism in it
  falls back, as everything unreadable does.

measure: a `get` lane against the plain field read, and a foldMap lane
  — the interpretation allocates a `Forget` per call and the fused
  form allocates nothing, so allocation is the number to watch.

teeth: the same poisoned-instance trick, on the Forget and Star
  interpretations this time.
